From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Attard <samuel.r.attard@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:00:28 +0000
Subject: gin: Take the callback by const reference in
 Invoker::DispatchToCallback

Invoker::DispatchToCallback took the base::RepeatingCallback by value,
so every call to a gin-bound function copied and destroyed it: one
atomic increment and one atomic decrement on the BindState refcount.
The callback is owned by the CallbackHolder for the lifetime of the
function template, so a const reference is enough.

Measured with a gin_unittests micro-benchmark (not part of this CL)
that calls a bound no-op void() 2e6 times from a JS loop, Linux x64
release build: 42.3 -> 32.1 ns per call.

No behaviour change.

Bug: None

Cherry-picked from
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8455325.
This patch can be removed when that CL lands and rolls into Electron.

diff --git a/gin/function_template.h b/gin/function_template.h
index 06c7ed637f5a7a60cf6251a20620df8c984f7402..19af32e0dc7b2c05d767bc6d54244c6c1c9ed8d2 100644
--- a/gin/function_template.h
+++ b/gin/function_template.h
@@ -209,7 +209,7 @@ class Invoker<std::index_sequence<indices...>, ArgTypes...>
 
   template <typename ReturnType>
   void DispatchToCallback(
-      base::RepeatingCallback<ReturnType(ArgTypes...)> callback) {
+      const base::RepeatingCallback<ReturnType(ArgTypes...)>& callback) {
     args_->Return(
         callback.Run(std::move(ArgumentHolder<indices, ArgTypes>::value)...));
   }
@@ -217,7 +217,8 @@ class Invoker<std::index_sequence<indices...>, ArgTypes...>
   // In C++, you can declare the function foo(void), but you can't pass a void
   // expression to foo. As a result, we must specialize the case of Callbacks
   // that have the void return type.
-  void DispatchToCallback(base::RepeatingCallback<void(ArgTypes...)> callback) {
+  void DispatchToCallback(
+      const base::RepeatingCallback<void(ArgTypes...)>& callback) {
     callback.Run(std::move(ArgumentHolder<indices, ArgTypes>::value)...);
   }
 
